Let
\[
\mathfrak R^Z_{n,d,\epsilon}
:=\inf_{\widehat\theta}
\sup_{P_Z\in\mathcal D_{d,\epsilon}}
E_{P_Z}\!\left[(\widehat\theta(\mathbf Z_n)-\theta_Z(P_Z))^2\right],
\]
where the infimum ranges over all possibly randomized estimators measurable with respect to \(\mathbf Z_n\) and auxiliary randomness independent of \(P_Z\).

Fix \(0<\epsilon<1/2\).  For each \(P_Z\in\mathcal D_{d,\epsilon}\), let \(\mathbf Z_n=((X_i,B_i^{\mathrm{obs}},Y_i))_{i=1}^n\) consist of \(n\) independent copies from \(P_Z\).  Given a realization \(\mathbf Z_n=((x_i,b_i,y_i))_{i=1}^n\), draw independent \(u_i\sim\operatorname{Bernoulli}(1/2)\), set
\[
o_i(u_i)=(x_i,u_i,0,1\{b_i=u_i\},1\{b_i=u_i\}y_i),             \tag{1}
\]
and define the explicit estimator
\[
\widehat\theta^{\mathrm{poly}}_{n,d,\epsilon}(\mathbf Z_n)
:=E_u\!\left[
\widehat\tau^{\mathrm{mix}}_{n,d,\epsilon}
\{o_1(u_1),\ldots,o_n(u_n)\}\mid\mathbf Z_n\right].           \tag{2}
\]
Then a universal \(\overline C<\infty\) satisfies
\[
\sup_{P_Z\in\mathcal D_{d,\epsilon}}
E_{P_Z}\!\left[
(\widehat\theta^{\mathrm{poly}}_{n,d,\epsilon}-\theta_Z(P_Z))^2
\right]
\le\overline C\min\left\{1,\frac1{n\epsilon}
+\left[\frac d{n\epsilon\log(e+n\epsilon)}\right]^2\right\}. \tag{3}
\]
Moreover, there are constants \(0<c_\epsilon\le C_\epsilon<\infty\), depending only on the fixed strict-interior \(\epsilon\), such that for every \(n,d\ge1\),
\[
c_\epsilon\min\left\{1,\frac1n+\left[\frac d{n\log(e+n)}\right]^2\right\}
\le\mathfrak R^Z_{n,d,\epsilon}
\le C_\epsilon\min\left\{1,\frac1n+\left[\frac d{n\log(e+n)}\right]^2\right\}. \tag{4}
\]
The assertion deliberately excludes \(\epsilon=1/2\).

Fix \(0<q<1/2\).  There are constants \(0<\underline c(q)\le\overline C(q)<\infty\), depending only on this fixed \(q\), such that for every \(n,d\ge1\),
\[
\underline c(q)
\min\left\{1,\frac1n+\left[\frac d{n\log(e+n)}\right]^2\right\}
\le \mathfrak R^{+}_{n,d,q}
\le \overline C(q)
\min\left\{1,\frac1n+\left[\frac d{n\log(e+n)}\right]^2\right\}.       \tag{1}
\]
Equivalently, in fixed-\(q\) comparison notation,
\[
\mathfrak R^{+}_{n,d,q}\asymp_q r_{n,d,q}.                                  \tag{2}
\]
The lower inequality is a point-risk transfer through the parameter-independent synthetic-assignment kernel in \(\mathrm{thm:zeng\mbox{-}fixed\mbox{-}positivity\mbox{-}polynomial\mbox{-}frontier}\).  Neither the constants are asserted to be uniform as \(q\downarrow0\), nor is a connected-confidence-interval lower bound asserted.
